config BR2_PACKAGE_STYX_RP1_CFE
	bool "styx-rp1-cfe"
	depends on BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	help
	  Styx's build of the Raspberry Pi 5 / CM5 camera receiver driver
	  (rp1-cfe-downstream): the image kernel's own driver plus a
	  mid-frame line event, which lets Styx process a frame in slices
	  during readout. Installed to /lib/modules/<release>/updates/,
	  where it takes precedence over the kernel's own
	  rp1-cfe-downstream.ko; the kernel itself is not changed. For Styx
	  images only (images using libcamera keep the stock driver).

	  The build fails when the kernel's own rp1_cfe sources are not the
	  ones the Styx driver was made from (re-import them:
	  kernel-modules/rp1-cfe).

comment "styx-rp1-cfe needs a Linux kernel to be built"
	depends on !BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
